WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.730
- It's time for Drew's Love Bug,

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:04.470
where we explore all things love

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:06.370
from dating to marriage,

00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:09.460
and certified dating coach
and our friend of the show,

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.670
Damona Hoffman is here,

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.880
and she and I have a lot to say today.

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.990
Hi Damona.
(crowd applauds)

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:16.190
- Hey Drew.

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:20.490
- Looking beautiful on the
inside and out as always.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.414
- Thank you (laughs).
- Okay.

00:00:22.414 --> 00:00:23.520
- I'm ready to help people in love.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:26.290
- I know, and you're, you
have been happily married

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:28.750
for a long time, and so, and you know,

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:32.130
I'm a divorcee, and I love
that we both come at it

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:35.440
from different points
of view, but I always

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:36.720
love your advice.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.330
It is so salient.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:40.950
It is just, I'm so happy to be a partner

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:42.630
in this with you,

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.930
because we're all contending
with relationships.

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.430
No matter what.
- Absolutely.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:49.040
- And so.
- Absolutely.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.100
And it can be really complicated
if we make it complicated.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.630
But I like to make it easy.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:56.210
And like you, I love love.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:58.360
- I absolutely love your approach,

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.110
and it should be easy, and actually,

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:02.830
okay, we're gonna get
right into questions,

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:05.760
because I'm just, I could
talk about this all day long.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.650
Okay, Shana is here,
and she has a question

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:08.943
about online dating.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:13.080
- Hi, so I jumped back
on the dating app Hinge,

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.040
which I had success within the past.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:18.450
Not really having success making
those quality connections.

00:01:18.450 --> 00:01:21.540
How do I move forward with initiating

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:24.923
the initial call or virtual
date without being super weird?

00:01:25.921 --> 00:01:27.140
- Damona.
(Damona laughs)

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.640
- Shana, it's only weird
if we make it weird.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.840
You, it sounds like you're
stuck in what I call

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:33.020
the texting trap.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:35.240
It's really easy to
think that you can filter

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.750
through all of these messages online,

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:40.060
but I want to help you break out of that.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:44.580
And you can do that by
inviting an invitation.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:45.880
And it doesn't have to be weird.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.400
You can just say, "I would
love to tell you more

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.730
about that when we meet for a date."

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:54.110
And then your man is
invited to pick up the phone

00:01:54.110 --> 00:01:56.150
or take you out on a date.

00:01:56.150 --> 00:01:57.770
Because we can sure waste a lot of time.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:01.610
So your love lesson Shana
is to not spend more

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:04.200
than one week after you match with someone

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:07.240
before you do a phone call or a date.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.105
That's it, that will
save you a lot of time,

00:02:09.105 --> 00:02:09.938
a lot of heartache.
- I love that.

00:02:09.938 --> 00:02:13.440
That is super amazing to
get a goal and a timeline.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.720
And Alex, if it's any consolation,

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.970
I tried a dating app,
and I got the same thing.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.030
No follow through.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:21.850
So Damona, I like your timeline.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:24.210
Shana, I'm so sorry, Alex is the one

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.840
who is actually coming here.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.160
We have a question from the fellas.

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:30.570
Alex is struggling to find the one.

00:02:30.570 --> 00:02:33.070
Alex, what's your question?

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.500
- Hey Drew Barrymore.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.670
So I feel like I'm Mr. Un-dateable.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.310
I've been burned a lot in the past.

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:41.410
And after a while, it, you know,

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:43.233
it's hard to stay the nice guy.

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.870
So my question is, you
know, how can I trust

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:49.180
and get back into the dating process again

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:51.620
after like a recent heartbreak
or rejection you know?

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:52.863
Am I un-dateable?

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:56.410
- I don't think so Drew.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:57.610
I think everyone is dateable,

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.820
and I think nice guys win.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:00.653
I married one.

00:03:00.653 --> 00:03:01.780
I did this whole dating plan

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.400
called Operation Date Nice Guys.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:04.920
I'll tell you about it another time.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:06.620
But here's the thing Alex.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.830
What happens when we have heartbreak

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:11.910
and when we have relationships
that don't work out,

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:15.050
we bring that pain with us
to the next relationship.

00:03:15.050 --> 00:03:17.500
And we put up these walls that prevent you

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:19.560
from really being yourself.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:21.110
And I don't know if you heard Alex,

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:24.190
but I would say that
vulnerability is the new black.

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:25.340
It's very sexy.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:28.540
So when you bring your
whole self into the room,

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.870
that's when you'll be
able to make your match.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.830
So here's your love lesson Alex.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:33.950
I would say try
- Okay.

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:36.760
- to take down those
walls without worrying

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:38.640
about the ultimate outcome,

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.440
because the ones who
are not right for you,

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:43.230
absolutely they will run for the hills.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.870
But the one who is right, and
we're only looking for one,

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.230
she will see all those
wonderful qualities about you.

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.800
- I totally agree Damona.

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.080
And you know what, I
promise you this Alex,

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:53.810
nice guys do finish last.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.500
So enjoy being single, because one day,

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:57.333
in an instant,
(fingers snap)

00:03:57.333 --> 00:03:59.450
it will be gone, and
you will find the girl

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:03.080
who realizes that when
it's nice, and less drama,

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.330
and really functioning, and you
guys have to work at things,

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.860
but it feels really right,

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:09.620
that is where we all end up.

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:12.520
And that is the right
place to be I believe.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:15.103
(upbeat music)

